IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- LAYER 1 -- Part 5A and Part 6 Chapter 1 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and
-- Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692), United Kingdom:
-- regs 45A to 52B (lines 1586-1788 of uksi-2017-692.txt).  The text is a plain-text rendering
-- made by a converter script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against
-- the official text.
--
-- WHAT THESE REGULATIONS DO.  Part 5A (requests for information about accounts and
-- safe-deposit boxes) is blank in this rendering.  Part 6 Chapter 1 puts duties on the
-- supervisors (supervisory authorities, self-regulatory organisations, the FCA, the Treasury):
-- to monitor, to share information, to co-operate, to keep what they learn confidential.  They
-- are encoded here for what they decide, and the seat layer asks them only as what they mean to a
-- business that is supervised.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  A function answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING.  NOTHING is "the
-- Regulations do not answer on these facts" and is never read as no.  Each function is named for
-- the proposition the provision itself states, in the provision's own polarity: a duty "is
-- discharged", a permission "may", a protection "is not to be taken to breach"; a prohibition is
-- named for the act it forbids and answers JUST FALSE where it applies (ruling N2).  A branch that
-- answers no carries FALSE-kind and the words that say no; a branch that answers "not covered"
-- carries NOTHING-kind and why.  Marginal readings (a), (b) and (c) are in NOTES.md.
--  * (a) a failed "if", "where", "when", "upon" or "provided that", a case outside a period the text
--    fixes in its own words, and a flat negative, answer JUST FALSE (rulings of 2026-11-05);
--  * (b) a grant or prohibition whose reach is limited by a relative clause or a class of persons,
--    with no "only", answers NOTHING outside the limit;
--  * (c) a duty ("must") that has not been discharged answers JUST FALSE.
-- Where a function named for the permitted act cannot say that an unmet condition leaves the
-- prohibition off (JUST FALSE would say the act is forbidden), a twin named for the prohibition
-- carries that answer (fork F10).
-- A fact a witness can state is a plain input.  An answer that belongs to another section or to
-- the keel is an input named for the section it comes from (a SEAM, PLAN.md section 5).

-- src:1586 | PART 5A — Requests for information about accounts and safe-deposit boxes
-- src:1587 | 45A Duty to establish mechanism for requests
-- src:1589 | 45B Duty to respond to requests for information
-- src:1591 | 45C Requests for information about accounts
-- src:1593 | 45D Requests for information about safe-deposit boxes
-- src:1595 | 45E Requirements for making a request for information
-- src:1597 | 45F Access to requests and responses, guidance and review
-- src:1599 | 45G Record keeping
-- src:1601 | 45H Interpretation
-- Regs 45A to 45H are headings, each followed by a line of dots: the text of Part 5A is blank in
-- this rendering.  Nothing is encoded for them (coverage rows: repealed or blank in this text).
-- The headings say only what the Part was about; this module does not guess what the removed
-- regulations required.

§ `Part 6 Chapter 1 -- Duties of supervisory authorities (regs 46 to 52B)`

-- Every act a supervisory authority, a self-regulatory organisation, the FCA or the Treasury is
-- asked to do by Chapter 1, named for its provision, for the regulative form of each duty.
DECLARE `reg 46 act of an authority` IS ONE OF
    `reg 46(1) monitor its own sector effectively and take necessary measures`
    `reg 46(2)(a) adopt a risk-based approach`
    `reg 46(2)(b) ensure access to relevant information on risks`
    `reg 46(2)(c) base the frequency and intensity of supervision on risk profiles`
    `reg 46(2)(d) keep a record in writing`
    `reg 46(2)(e) take effective measures to encourage reporting of breaches`
    `reg 46(2)(f) provide secure communication channels`
    `reg 46(2)(g) take reasonable measures to protect the reporting person's identity`
    `reg 46(3)(b) take account of the degree of discretion permitted to relevant persons`
    `reg 46(4) review risk assessments and the adequacy of policies`
    `reg 46(5) inform the NCA`
    `reg 46(8)(a) monitor the auction platform's compliance`
    `reg 46A publish an annual report`
    `reg 47(1) make up-to-date information available`
    `reg 48(1) give guidance on politically exposed persons`
    `reg 49(1) make arrangements to ensure the matters listed`
    `reg 49(2)(a) provide adequate resources`
    `reg 49(2)(b) appoint a person to monitor and manage the organisation's compliance`
    `reg 49(3)(b) ensure the organisation responds fully and rapidly to requests for information`
    `reg 50(1) co-operate and co-ordinate`
    `reg 51(1) collect information`
    `reg 51(2) provide the Treasury with information on request`
    `reg 51(3) publish an annual consolidated review`

§§ `Regulation 46 -- Duties of supervisory authorities`

-- Which authority's "own sector" a relevant person is in.  "A supervisory authority must
-- effectively monitor the relevant persons for which it is the supervisory authority".
-- src:1606 | (1) A supervisory authority must effectively monitor the relevant persons for which it is the supervisory authority (“its own sector”) and take necessary measures for the purpose of —
-- src:1607 | (a) securing compliance by such persons with the requirements of these Regulations; and
-- src:1608 | (b) securing that any application for which the supervisory authority grants approval under regulation 26 meets the requirements of regulation 26(7), whether or not the person making the application, or being approved, is a relevant person.
@ref reg 46(1) (src:1606-1608)
-- SEAM S-K3 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 7(1) the supervisory authorities of the relevant person` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF Authority) -- the keel's reg 7(1) answer
      `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(1) the authority must monitor the relevant person as part of its own sector` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 7(1) the supervisory authorities of the relevant person`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which authority supervises the relevant person is reg 7's answer and it has not been given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST authorities THEN
        IF elem `the authority` authorities
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the relevant persons for which it is the supervisory authority" is a scope limit with no "only"
        ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 46(1) (src:1606-1608)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(1) the authority must monitor its own sector effectively (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(1) monitor its own sector effectively and take necessary measures`

-- "necessary measures for the purpose of (a) securing compliance by such persons with the
-- requirements of these Regulations".
@ref reg 46(1)(a) (src:1607)
GIVEN `it took the measures that were necessary to secure compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(1)(a) the authority has taken necessary measures for the purpose of securing compliance` MEANS
    IF `it took the measures that were necessary to secure compliance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" -- an undischarged duty (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "(b) securing that any application for which the supervisory authority grants approval under
-- regulation 26 meets the requirements of regulation 26(7), whether or not the person making the
-- application, or being approved, is a relevant person".  SEAM S-11 is reg 26(7)'s answer.
@ref reg 46(1)(b) (src:1608)
-- SEAM S-11 (asking)
GIVEN `the authority granted approval under regulation 26` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 26(7) the application for approval meets the requirements of regulation 26(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(1)(b) the application approved under regulation 26 meets the requirements of regulation 26(7)` MEANS
    IF `the authority granted approval under regulation 26`
    THEN CONSIDER `reg 26(7) the application for approval meets the requirements of regulation 26(7)`
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the application meets reg 26(7) is that regulation's answer and it has not been given
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" -- an approved application that does not meet reg 26(7) is a duty not discharged (Marginal readings, (c))
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any application for which the supervisory authority grants approval" -- no approval, no application in scope
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "whether or not the person making the application, or being approved, is a relevant person": the
-- status of that person makes no difference, so this twin takes it as an input and gives the same
-- answer for either value.
@ref reg 46(1)(b) (src:1608)
GIVEN `the person making the application, or being approved, is a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority granted approval under regulation 26` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 26(7) the application for approval meets the requirements of regulation 26(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(1)(b) whether or not the person is a relevant person, the application approved under regulation 26 meets the requirements of regulation 26(7)` MEANS
    `reg 46(1)(b) the application approved under regulation 26 meets the requirements of regulation 26(7)` `the authority granted approval under regulation 26` `reg 26(7) the application for approval meets the requirements of regulation 26(7)`

-- src:1610 | (a) adopt a risk-based approach to the exercise of its supervisory functions, informed by the risk assessments carried out by the authority under regulation 17;
@ref reg 46(2)(a) (src:1610)
GIVEN `it has adopted a risk-based approach to the exercise of its supervisory functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that approach is informed by the risk assessments it carried out under regulation 17` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(2)(a) the authority has adopted a risk-based approach informed by its risk assessments` MEANS
    IF `it has adopted a risk-based approach to the exercise of its supervisory functions`
       AND `that approach is informed by the risk assessments it carried out under regulation 17`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" -- an undischarged duty (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(2)(a) (src:1610)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(2)(a) the authority must adopt a risk-based approach (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(2)(a) adopt a risk-based approach`

-- src:1611 | (b) ensure that its employees and officers have access both at its offices and elsewhere to relevant information on the domestic and international risks of money laundering and terrorist financing which affect its own sector;
@ref reg 46(2)(b) (src:1611)
GIVEN `its employees and officers have access to relevant information at its offices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its employees and officers have access to relevant information elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(2)(b) the authority has ensured access to relevant information on the risks` MEANS
    IF `its employees and officers have access to relevant information at its offices`
       AND `its employees and officers have access to relevant information elsewhere`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" -- "access both at its offices and elsewhere" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(2)(b) (src:1611)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(2)(b) the authority must ensure access to relevant information (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(2)(b) ensure access to relevant information on risks`

-- src:1612 | (c) base the frequency and intensity of its on-site and off-site supervision on the risk profiles prepared under regulation 17(4);
@ref reg 46(2)(c) (src:1612)
GIVEN `it bases the frequency of its on-site and off-site supervision on the risk profiles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it bases the intensity of its on-site and off-site supervision on the risk profiles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(2)(c) the authority bases the frequency and intensity of supervision on the risk profiles prepared under regulation 17(4)` MEANS
    IF `it bases the frequency of its on-site and off-site supervision on the risk profiles`
       AND `it bases the intensity of its on-site and off-site supervision on the risk profiles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(2)(c) (src:1612)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(2)(c) the authority must base the frequency and intensity of supervision on risk profiles (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(2)(c) base the frequency and intensity of supervision on risk profiles`

-- "(d) keep a record in writing of the actions it has taken in the course of its supervision,
-- and of its reasons for deciding not to act in a particular case".  The reasons need recording
-- only for a case in which it decided not to act.
-- src:1613 | (d) keep a record in writing of the actions it has taken in the course of its supervision, and of its reasons for deciding not to act in a particular case;
@ref reg 46(2)(d) (src:1613)
GIVEN `it keeps a written record of the actions it has taken in the course of its supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has decided not to act in a particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it keeps a written record of its reasons for deciding not to act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(2)(d) the authority keeps a record in writing of its actions and of its reasons for deciding not to act` MEANS
    IF `it keeps a written record of the actions it has taken in the course of its supervision`
       AND ((NOT `it has decided not to act in a particular case`) OR `it keeps a written record of its reasons for deciding not to act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(2)(d) (src:1613)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(2)(d) the authority must keep a record in writing (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(2)(d) keep a record in writing`

-- src:1614 | (e) take effective measures to encourage its own sector to report actual or potential breaches of the provisions of these Regulations to it;
@ref reg 46(2)(e) (src:1614)
GIVEN `it takes effective measures to encourage its own sector to report actual or potential breaches` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(2)(e) the authority takes effective measures to encourage its own sector to report breaches` MEANS
    IF `it takes effective measures to encourage its own sector to report actual or potential breaches`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(2)(e) (src:1614)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(2)(e) the authority must encourage reporting of breaches (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(2)(e) take effective measures to encourage reporting of breaches`

-- "(f) provide one or more secure communication channels": one or more is at least one.
-- src:1615 | (f) provide one or more secure communication channels for persons to report actual or potential breaches of these Regulations to it;
@ref reg 46(2)(f) (src:1615)
GIVEN `the number of secure communication channels it provides for reporting breaches` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(2)(f) the authority provides one or more secure communication channels for reporting breaches` MEANS
    IF `the number of secure communication channels it provides for reporting breaches` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "one or more" -- none is a duty not discharged (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(2)(f) (src:1615)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(2)(f) the authority must provide secure communication channels (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(2)(f) provide secure communication channels`

-- src:1616 | (g) take reasonable measures to ensure that the identity of the reporting person is known only to the supervisory authority.
@ref reg 46(2)(g) (src:1616)
GIVEN `it takes reasonable measures to ensure that the identity of the reporting person is known only to the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(2)(g) the authority takes reasonable measures to ensure that the identity of the reporting person is known only to it` MEANS
    IF `it takes reasonable measures to ensure that the identity of the reporting person is known only to the authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(2)(g) (src:1616)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(2)(g) the authority must protect the reporting person's identity (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(2)(g) take reasonable measures to protect the reporting person's identity`

-- Reg 46(3)(a) is blank in this rendering (a line of dots).
-- src:1617 | (3) In determining its approach to the exercise of its supervisory functions the supervisory authority must—
-- src:1618 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1619 | (b) take account of the degree of discretion permitted to relevant persons in taking measures to counter money laundering and terrorist financing.
@ref reg 46(3)(b) (src:1617-1619)
GIVEN `it has taken account of the degree of discretion permitted to relevant persons in taking measures to counter money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(3)(b) the authority has taken account of the degree of discretion permitted to relevant persons` MEANS
    IF `it has taken account of the degree of discretion permitted to relevant persons in taking measures to counter money laundering and terrorist financing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(3)(b) (src:1619)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(3)(b) the authority must take account of the degree of discretion (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(3)(b) take account of the degree of discretion permitted to relevant persons`

-- "In accordance with its risk-based approach, the supervisory authority must take appropriate
-- measures to review (a) the risk assessments carried out by relevant persons under regulation 18".
-- src:1620 | (4) In accordance with its risk-based approach, the supervisory authority must take appropriate measures to review—
-- src:1621 | (a) the risk assessments carried out by relevant persons under regulation 18;
@ref reg 46(4)(a) (src:1620-1621)
GIVEN `it takes appropriate measures to review the risk assessments carried out by relevant persons under regulation 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(4)(a) the authority takes appropriate measures to review the risk assessments carried out by relevant persons` MEANS
    IF `it takes appropriate measures to review the risk assessments carried out by relevant persons under regulation 18`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "(b) the adequacy of the policies, controls and procedures adopted by relevant persons under
-- regulation 19 to 21 and 24, and the way in which those policies, controls and procedures have
-- been implemented": two things to review, the adequacy and the implementation.
-- src:1620 | (4) In accordance with its risk-based approach, the supervisory authority must take appropriate measures to review—
-- src:1622 | (b) the adequacy of the policies, controls and procedures adopted by relevant persons under regulation 19 to 21 and 24, and the way in which those policies, controls and procedures have been implemented.
@ref reg 46(4)(b) (src:1620-1622)
GIVEN `it takes appropriate measures to review the adequacy of the policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it takes appropriate measures to review the way in which they have been implemented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(4)(b) the authority takes appropriate measures to review the adequacy and implementation of policies, controls and procedures` MEANS
    IF `it takes appropriate measures to review the adequacy of the policies, controls and procedures`
       AND `it takes appropriate measures to review the way in which they have been implemented`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(4) (src:1620-1622)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(4) the authority must review the risk assessments and the adequacy of policies (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(4) review risk assessments and the adequacy of policies`

-- "A supervisory authority which, in the course of carrying out any of its supervisory functions
-- or otherwise, knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a
-- person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing must as soon as
-- practicable inform the NCA."  Whether it knows or suspects is a fact the authority states.
-- src:1623 | (5) A supervisory authority which, in the course of carrying out any of its supervisory functions or otherwise, knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing must as soon as practicable inform the NCA.
@ref reg 46(5) (src:1623)
GIVEN `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(5) the authority must inform the NCA` MEANS
    IF `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A supervisory authority which ... knows or suspects" is a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "as soon as practicable" is a period the text leaves to judgement, so it is a plain input.
@ref reg 46(5) (src:1623)
GIVEN `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has informed the NCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it informed the NCA as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(5) the authority has informed the NCA as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A supervisory authority which ... knows or suspects" is a scope limit with no "only"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it has informed the NCA` AND `it informed the NCA as soon as practicable`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must as soon as practicable inform the NCA" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(5) (src:1623)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(5) the authority must inform the NCA (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(5) inform the NCA`

-- "A disclosure made under paragraph (5) is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however
-- imposed, on the disclosure of information."  TRUE: the protection is given.
-- src:1624 | (6) A disclosure made under paragraph (5) is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information.
@ref reg 46(6) (src:1624)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(6) the disclosure is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A disclosure made under paragraph (5)" -- a disclosure made otherwise is outside the protection and the paragraph says nothing of it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "Where a disclosure under paragraph (5) is made in good faith, no civil liability arises in
-- respect of the disclosure on the part of the person by whom, or on whose behalf, it is made."
-- src:1625 | (7) Where a disclosure under paragraph (5) is made in good faith, no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person by whom, or on whose behalf, it is made.
@ref reg 46(7) (src:1625)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(7) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person who made it` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)` AND `it was made in good faith`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a disclosure under paragraph (5) is made in good faith" -- the condition is not met, so this paragraph's protection does not apply (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); Marginal readings, (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The FCA in relation to an auction platform.
-- src:1626 | (8) The FCA, when carrying out its supervisory functions in relation to an auction platform—
-- src:1627 | (a) must effectively monitor the auction platform's compliance with—
-- src:1628 | (i) the customer due diligence requirements of regulation 17 of the UK auctioning regulations;
-- src:1629 | (ii) the monitoring and record-keeping requirements of regulation 37 of those Regulations; and
-- src:1630 | (iii) the notification requirements of regulation 38(4) and (5) of those Regulations; and
@ref reg 46(8)(a) (src:1626-1630)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
      `it is carrying out its supervisory functions in relation to an auction platform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(8)(a) the authority must effectively monitor the auction platform's compliance` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the authority` EQUALS `the Financial Conduct Authority`))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The FCA" -- another authority is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it is carrying out its supervisory functions in relation to an auction platform`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when carrying out its supervisory functions in relation to an auction platform" -- "when" counts as "where", and the occasion is not met (delegated reading (c) of 2026-11-05)
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(8)(a)(i) to (iii) (src:1627-1630)
GIVEN `it monitors the auction platform's compliance with the customer due diligence requirements of regulation 17 of the UK auctioning regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it monitors the auction platform's compliance with the monitoring and record-keeping requirements of regulation 37 of those Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it monitors the auction platform's compliance with the notification requirements of regulation 38(4) and (5) of those Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(8)(a) the FCA has monitored the auction platform's compliance with all three sets of requirements` MEANS
    IF `it monitors the auction platform's compliance with the customer due diligence requirements of regulation 17 of the UK auctioning regulations`
       AND `it monitors the auction platform's compliance with the monitoring and record-keeping requirements of regulation 37 of those Regulations`
       AND `it monitors the auction platform's compliance with the notification requirements of regulation 38(4) and (5) of those Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must effectively monitor" -- limbs (i), (ii) and (iii) (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46(8)(a) (src:1626-1630)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46(8)(a) the FCA must effectively monitor the auction platform's compliance (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46(8)(a) monitor the auction platform's compliance`

-- "(b) may monitor the auction platform's compliance with regulations 18 to 21 and 24 of these
-- Regulations": a permission of the same authority on the same occasion.
-- src:1631 | (b) may monitor the auction platform's compliance with regulations 18 to 21 and 24 of these Regulations.
@ref reg 46(8)(b) (src:1631)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
      `it is carrying out its supervisory functions in relation to an auction platform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(8)(b) the authority may monitor the auction platform's compliance with regulations 18 to 21 and 24` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the authority` EQUALS `the Financial Conduct Authority`))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The FCA" -- another authority is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it is carrying out its supervisory functions in relation to an auction platform`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when carrying out its supervisory functions in relation to an auction platform" -- "when" counts as "where", and the occasion is not met (delegated reading (c) of 2026-11-05)
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "The functions of the FCA under these Regulations shall be treated for the purposes of Parts 1,
-- 2 and 4 of Schedule 1ZA to FSMA ... as functions conferred on the FCA under that Act."
-- src:1632 | (9) The functions of the FCA under these Regulations shall be treated for the purposes of Parts 1, 2 and 4 of Schedule 1ZA to FSMA (the Financial Conduct Authority) as functions conferred on the FCA under that Act.
@ref reg 46(9) (src:1632)
GIVEN `the function is a function of the FCA under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46(9) the function is treated as a function conferred on the FCA under FSMA for the purposes of Parts 1, 2 and 4 of Schedule 1ZA` MEANS
    IF `the function is a function of the FCA under these Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The functions of the FCA under these Regulations" -- any other function is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 46A -- Annual reports by self-regulatory organisations`

-- src:1634 | A self-regulatory organisation must publish or make arrangements to publish an annual report containing information about—
-- src:1635 | (a) measures taken by the self-regulatory organisation to encourage the reporting of actual or potential breaches as referred to in regulation 46(2)(e);
-- src:1636 | (b) the number of reports of actual or potential breaches received by that self-regulatory organisation as referred to in regulation 46(2)(e);
-- src:1637 | (c) the number and description of measures carried out by the self-regulatory organisation to monitor, and enforce, compliance by relevant persons with their obligations under—
-- src:1638 | (i) Part 3 (customer due diligence);
-- src:1639 | (ii) Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 (terrorist property) and Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (money laundering) ;
-- src:1640 | (iii) regulation 40 (record-keeping); and
-- src:1641 | (iv) regulations 20 to 24 (policies and controls etc.).
@ref reg 46A (src:1634-1641)
GIVEN `the body is a self-regulatory organisation` IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 3(1), a fact
      `it has published or made arrangements to publish an annual report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains information about the measures it has taken to encourage the reporting of breaches (regulation 46(2)(e))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains information about the number of reports of breaches it has received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains the number and description of measures to monitor and enforce compliance with Part 3 (customer due diligence)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains the number and description of measures to monitor and enforce compliance with Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 and Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains the number and description of measures to monitor and enforce compliance with regulation 40 (record-keeping)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains the number and description of measures to monitor and enforce compliance with regulations 20 to 24 (policies and controls etc.)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 46A the self-regulatory organisation has published an annual report containing the required information` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the body is a self-regulatory organisation`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A self-regulatory organisation must ..." -- another body is outside the regulation
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it has published or made arrangements to publish an annual report`
            AND `the report contains information about the measures it has taken to encourage the reporting of breaches (regulation 46(2)(e))`
            AND `the report contains information about the number of reports of breaches it has received`
            AND `the report contains the number and description of measures to monitor and enforce compliance with Part 3 (customer due diligence)`
            AND `the report contains the number and description of measures to monitor and enforce compliance with Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 and Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002`
            AND `the report contains the number and description of measures to monitor and enforce compliance with regulation 40 (record-keeping)`
            AND `the report contains the number and description of measures to monitor and enforce compliance with regulations 20 to 24 (policies and controls etc.)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must publish or make arrangements to publish an annual report containing information about" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 46A (src:1634)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 46A the self-regulatory organisation must publish an annual report (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 46A publish an annual report`

§§ `Regulation 47 -- Duties of supervisory authorities: information`

-- src:1643 | (1) A supervisory authority must, in any way it considers appropriate, make up-to-date information on money laundering and terrorist financing available to those relevant persons which it supervises (“its own sector”).
@ref reg 47(1) (src:1643)
-- SEAM S-K3 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 7(1) the supervisory authorities of the relevant person` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF Authority)
      `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 47(1) the authority must make up-to-date information available to the relevant person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 7(1) the supervisory authorities of the relevant person`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which authority supervises the relevant person is reg 7's answer and it has not been given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST authorities THEN
        IF elem `the authority` authorities
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "those relevant persons which it supervises" is a scope limit with no "only"
        ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 47(1) (src:1643)
GIVEN `it has made up-to-date information on money laundering and terrorist financing available, in a way it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 47(1) the authority has made up-to-date information on money laundering and terrorist financing available` MEANS
    IF `it has made up-to-date information on money laundering and terrorist financing available, in a way it considers appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 47(1) (src:1643)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 47(1) the authority must make up-to-date information available (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 47(1) make up-to-date information available`

-- src:1644 | (2) The information referred to in paragraph (1) must include the following—
-- src:1645 | (a) information on the money laundering and terrorist financing practices considered by the supervisory authority to apply to its own sector;
-- src:1646 | (b) a description of indications which may suggest that a transfer of criminal funds is taking place in its own sector;
-- src:1647 | (c) a description of the circumstances in which the supervisory authority considers that there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing.
@ref reg 47(2) (src:1644-1647)
GIVEN `the information includes the money laundering and terrorist financing practices the authority considers to apply to its own sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes a description of indications which may suggest that a transfer of criminal funds is taking place in its own sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes a description of the circumstances in which the authority considers that there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 47(2) the information includes the three matters the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the information includes the money laundering and terrorist financing practices the authority considers to apply to its own sector`
       AND `the information includes a description of indications which may suggest that a transfer of criminal funds is taking place in its own sector`
       AND `the information includes a description of the circumstances in which the authority considers that there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must include the following" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Reg 47(3)(a) to (e) are blank in this rendering (lines of dots).  The three sources that
-- remain are (f), (g) and (h); each is owed only if the authority considers it relevant to its
-- own sector, a judgement the text hands to the authority and so a plain input.
-- src:1648 | (3) The information referred to in paragraph (1) must also include information from the following sources which the supervisory authority considers is relevant to its own sector—
-- src:1654 | (f) the report prepared by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(6);
@ref reg 47(3)(f) (src:1648-1654)
GIVEN `the authority considers the report relevant to its own sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes the report prepared by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 47(3)(f) the information includes the report prepared by the Treasury and the Home Office` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the authority considers the report relevant to its own sector`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which the supervisory authority considers is relevant to its own sector" -- a source it does not consider relevant is outside the duty
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the information includes the report prepared by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(6)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must also include information from the following sources" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1655 | (g) any relevant information made available by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(8);
@ref reg 47(3)(g) (src:1655)
GIVEN `the authority considers the information relevant to its own sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes any relevant information made available by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 47(3)(g) the information includes the relevant information made available by the Treasury and the Home Office` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the authority considers the information relevant to its own sector`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which the supervisory authority considers is relevant to its own sector" -- a source it does not consider relevant is outside the duty
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the information includes any relevant information made available by the Treasury and the Home Office under regulation 16(8)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must also include information from the following sources" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1656 | (h) any relevant information published by the Director General of the NCA under section 4(9) (operations) or 6 (duty to publish information) of the Crime and Courts Act 2013 .
@ref reg 47(3)(h) (src:1656)
GIVEN `the authority considers the information relevant to its own sector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes any relevant information published by the Director General of the NCA under section 4(9) or 6 of the Crime and Courts Act 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 47(3)(h) the information includes the relevant information published by the Director General of the NCA` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the authority considers the information relevant to its own sector`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which the supervisory authority considers is relevant to its own sector" -- a source it does not consider relevant is outside the duty
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the information includes any relevant information published by the Director General of the NCA under section 4(9) or 6 of the Crime and Courts Act 2013`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must also include information from the following sources" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 48 -- Duties of the FCA: guidance on politically exposed persons`

-- src:1658 | (1) The FCA must give guidance under section 139A of FSMA (power of the FCA to give guidance) to relevant persons, who are subject to rules made by the FCA, in relation to the enhanced customer due diligence measures required under regulation 35 in respect of politically exposed persons (“PEPs”), their family members and known close associates (within the meanings given in regulation 35(12)).
@ref reg 48(1) (src:1658)
GIVEN `the relevant person is subject to rules made by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 48(1) the FCA must give the relevant person guidance on enhanced customer due diligence measures for politically exposed persons` MEANS
    IF `the relevant person is subject to rules made by the FCA`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to relevant persons, who are subject to rules made by the FCA" -- a relevant person not subject to FCA rules is outside the duty
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The same duty asked of a given authority: only the FCA is named, so another authority (the
-- Commissioners, for one) is outside the paragraph.
@ref reg 48(1) (src:1658)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
      `the relevant person is subject to rules made by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 48(1) the authority must give the relevant person guidance on enhanced customer due diligence measures for politically exposed persons` MEANS
    IF `the authority` EQUALS `the Financial Conduct Authority`
    THEN `reg 48(1) the FCA must give the relevant person guidance on enhanced customer due diligence measures for politically exposed persons` `the relevant person is subject to rules made by the FCA`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The FCA must give guidance" -- another authority is outside the paragraph and the Regulations name no duty for it
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 48(1) (src:1658)
GIVEN `the FCA has given guidance under section 139A of FSMA on the enhanced customer due diligence measures required under regulation 35` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 48(1) the FCA has given guidance on politically exposed persons, their family members and known close associates` MEANS
    IF `the FCA has given guidance under section 139A of FSMA on the enhanced customer due diligence measures required under regulation 35`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give guidance" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 48(1) (src:1658)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 48(1) the FCA must give guidance on politically exposed persons (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 48(1) give guidance on politically exposed persons`

DECLARE `reg 48(2) matter on which the guidance must include guidance` IS ONE OF
    `reg 48(2)(a) what functions are, and are not, prominent public functions`
    `reg 48(2)(b) which persons are family members of a politically exposed person or known close associates of one`
    `reg 48(2)(c) what constitutes appropriate risk-management systems and procedures`
    `reg 48(2)(d) what account is to be taken of the jurisdiction in which the prominent public function arises`
    `reg 48(2)(e) how the level of risk associated with a particular individual is to be assessed`
    `reg 48(2)(f) who should be treated as senior management`
    `reg 48(2)(g) when senior management approval may be given by an individual who is not a member of the board`
    `reg 48(2)(h) what constitutes adequate measures and reasonable measures`
    `reg 48(2)(i) the extent to which information on public registers may be taken into account`
    `reg 48(2)(j) what sort of monitoring and scrutiny is required`
    `reg 48(2)(k) what measures are required for persons who have ceased to be politically exposed persons`
    `reg 48(2)(l) how to address risks where a politically exposed person, a family member or a known close associate is a beneficial owner or a beneficiary`

-- The list is the paragraph's, in its order: "(a)" to "(l)".
-- src:1659 | (2) The guidance referred to in paragraph (1) must include guidance on the following matters—
-- src:1660 | (a) taking into account regulation 35(14), what functions are, and are not, to be taken to be “prominent public functions” for the purposes of determining whether an individual is a PEP;
-- src:1661 | (b) which persons should be treated as coming within the definitions of—
-- src:1662 | (i) a family member of a PEP; or
-- src:1663 | (ii) a known close associate of a PEP;
-- src:1664 | (c) what constitutes “appropriate risk-management systems and procedures” for the purposes of regulation 35(1);
-- src:1665 | (d) what account is to be taken of the jurisdiction in which the prominent public function arises (taking into consideration the controls against money-laundering and terrorist financing in different jurisdictions);
-- src:1666 | (e) how the level of risk associated with a particular individual is to be assessed for the purposes of regulation 35(3), and what approach is to be taken in relation to a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP, if the PEP, family member or close associate is assessed as presenting a low level of risk;
-- src:1667 | (f) who should be treated as coming within the meaning of “senior management” for the purposes of regulation 35(5) and (8);
-- src:1668 | (g) the situations in which it would be appropriate for the senior management approval mentioned in regulation 35(5) to be given by an individual who is not a member of the board of directors (or, if there is no such board, a member of the equivalent management body) of a business;
-- src:1669 | (h) what constitutes “adequate measures” and “reasonable measures” for the purposes of paragraphs (5) and (6) respectively of regulation 35;
-- src:1670 | (i) the extent to which information on public registers may be taken into account for the purposes of regulation 35(5) and (6);
-- src:1671 | (j) what sort of monitoring and scrutiny is required for the purposes of regulation 35(5) and (8);
-- src:1672 | (k) what measures are required in relation to persons who have ceased to be PEPs to comply with regulation 35(9); and
-- src:1673 | (l) how to address risks of money laundering or terrorist financing where a PEP, a family member of a PEP or a known close associate of a PEP, is—
-- src:1674 | (i) the beneficial owner of a customer;
-- src:1675 | (ii) a beneficiary of a contract of long-term insurance;
-- src:1676 | (iii) the beneficial owner of a beneficiary of a contract of long-term insurance.
@ref reg 48(2) (src:1659-1676)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 48(2) matter on which the guidance must include guidance`
`reg 48(2) the matters on which the guidance must include guidance` MEANS
    LIST `reg 48(2)(a) what functions are, and are not, prominent public functions`
       , `reg 48(2)(b) which persons are family members of a politically exposed person or known close associates of one`
       , `reg 48(2)(c) what constitutes appropriate risk-management systems and procedures`
       , `reg 48(2)(d) what account is to be taken of the jurisdiction in which the prominent public function arises`
       , `reg 48(2)(e) how the level of risk associated with a particular individual is to be assessed`
       , `reg 48(2)(f) who should be treated as senior management`
       , `reg 48(2)(g) when senior management approval may be given by an individual who is not a member of the board`
       , `reg 48(2)(h) what constitutes adequate measures and reasonable measures`
       , `reg 48(2)(i) the extent to which information on public registers may be taken into account`
       , `reg 48(2)(j) what sort of monitoring and scrutiny is required`
       , `reg 48(2)(k) what measures are required for persons who have ceased to be politically exposed persons`
       , `reg 48(2)(l) how to address risks where a politically exposed person, a family member or a known close associate is a beneficial owner or a beneficiary`

@ref reg 48(2) (src:1659)
GIVEN `the matters the guidance covers` IS A LIST OF `reg 48(2) matter on which the guidance must include guidance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 48(2) the guidance includes guidance on every one of the matters` MEANS
    IF all (GIVEN matter YIELD elem matter `the matters the guidance covers`) `reg 48(2) the matters on which the guidance must include guidance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must include guidance on the following matters" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 49 -- Duties of self-regulatory organisations`

-- src:1678 | (1) Self-regulatory organisations must make arrangements to ensure that—
-- src:1679 | (a) their supervisory functions are exercised independently of any of their other functions which do not relate to disciplinary matters;
