    IF `it has made arrangements to ensure that it employs only persons with appropriate qualifications, integrity and professional skills to carry out the supervisory functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must make arrangements to ensure that" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1682 | (d) contravention of a relevant requirement by a relevant person they are responsible for supervising renders that person liable to effective, proportionate and dissuasive disciplinary measures under their rules;
@ref reg 49(1)(d) (src:1682)
GIVEN `it has made arrangements to ensure that a contravention of a relevant requirement renders the relevant person liable to effective, proportionate and dissuasive disciplinary measures under its rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 49(1)(d) the self-regulatory organisation has made arrangements to ensure that a contravention renders the person liable to disciplinary measures` MEANS
    IF `it has made arrangements to ensure that a contravention of a relevant requirement renders the relevant person liable to effective, proportionate and dissuasive disciplinary measures under its rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must make arrangements to ensure that" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- What the arrangement means to the relevant person: "contravention of a relevant requirement by
-- a relevant person they are responsible for supervising renders that person liable".  The
-- relevant requirement is a borrowed term (reg 3(1) and reg 75), so it is a plain fact.
@ref reg 49(1)(d) (src:1682)
GIVEN `the relevant person is one the self-regulatory organisation is responsible for supervising` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has contravened a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 49(1)(d) the relevant person is liable to effective, proportionate and dissuasive disciplinary measures under the organisation's rules` MEANS
    IF `the relevant person is one the self-regulatory organisation is responsible for supervising` AND `the relevant person has contravened a relevant requirement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "contravention of a relevant requirement by a relevant person they are responsible for supervising" -- no contravention, or a person it does not supervise, is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1683 | (e) potential conflicts of interest within the organisation are appropriately handled.
@ref reg 49(1)(e) (src:1683)
GIVEN `it has made arrangements to ensure that potential conflicts of interest within the organisation are appropriately handled` IS A BOOLEAN
