-- "The person appointed under paragraph (2)(b) is to be responsible (a) for liaison with (i)
-- another supervisory authority or a registering authority (within the meaning of regulation
-- 53); (ii) any law enforcement authority; and (iii) any overseas authority (within the meaning
-- of regulation 50(4))".  SEAM S-15 is reg 44(10)'s answer on a law enforcement authority.
-- src:1687 | (3) The person appointed under paragraph (2)(b) is to be responsible—
-- src:1688 | (a) for liaison with—
-- src:1689 | (i) another supervisory authority or a registering authority (within the meaning of regulation 53);
-- src:1690 | (ii) any law enforcement authority; and
-- src:1691 | (iii) any overseas authority (within the meaning of regulation 50(4))
@ref reg 49(3)(a) (src:1687-1691)
-- SEAM S-15 (asking)
GIVEN `the body is another supervisory authority or a registering authority within the meaning of regulation 53` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body is an overseas authority within the meaning of regulation 50(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 49(3)(a) the person appointed is responsible for liaison with the body` MEANS
    IF `the body is another supervisory authority or a registering authority within the meaning of regulation 53`
       OR `the body is an overseas authority within the meaning of regulation 50(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a law enforcement authority is reg 44(10)'s answer and it has not been given
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): (i) to (iii) say who the person liaises with and do not say that no one else is a body to liaise with
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING

-- "(b) for ensuring that the self-regulatory organisation responds fully and rapidly to any
-- request from an authority referred to in paragraph (a)(i) or (ii) for information about any
-- person it supervises, whether that request concerns an application by that person for
-- registration or any other matter."
-- src:1692 | (b) for ensuring that the self-regulatory organisation responds fully and rapidly to any request from an authority referred to in paragraph (a)(i) or (ii) for information about any person it supervises, whether that request concerns an application by that person for registration or any other matter.
@ref reg 49(3)(b) (src:1692)
-- SEAM S-15 (asking)
GIVEN `the request comes from another supervisory authority or a registering authority within the meaning of regulation 53` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the request is for information about a person the organisation supervises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organisation has responded fully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organisation has responded rapidly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 49(3)(b) the self-regulatory organisation has responded fully and rapidly to the request` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the request is for information about a person the organisation supervises`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any request ... for information about any person it supervises" -- another request is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the request comes from another supervisory authority or a registering authority within the meaning of regulation 53`
            OR `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN IF `the organisation has responded fully` AND `the organisation has responded rapidly`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "responds fully and rapidly" (Marginal readings, (c))
              ELSE JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an authority referred to in paragraph (a)(i) or (ii)" -- a request from another body, or from a body whose standing as a law enforcement authority is not answered, is outside the paragraph
         ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 49(3)(b) (src:1692)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 49(3)(b) the person appointed must ensure that the organisation responds fully and rapidly (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 49(3)(b) ensure the organisation responds fully and rapidly to requests for information`

§§ `Regulation 50 -- Duty to co-operate`

-- Reg 50(1)(c) is blank in this rendering.  "such steps as it considers appropriate" hands a
-- judgement to the authority, so the input is that the authority has taken the steps it
-- considers appropriate.
-- src:1694 | (1) A supervisory authority must take such steps as it considers appropriate—
-- src:1695 | (a) to co-operate with other supervisory authorities, the Treasury , the registrar and law enforcement authorities in relation to the development and implementation of policies to counter money laundering and terrorist financing;
@ref reg 50(1)(a) (src:1694-1695)
GIVEN `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with other supervisory authorities, the Treasury, the registrar and law enforcement authorities in the development and implementation of policies to counter money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 50(1)(a) the authority has taken the steps it considers appropriate to co-operate` MEANS
    IF `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with other supervisory authorities, the Treasury, the registrar and law enforcement authorities in the development and implementation of policies to counter money laundering and terrorist financing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take such steps as it considers appropriate" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1694 | (1) A supervisory authority must take such steps as it considers appropriate—
-- src:1696 | (b) to co-ordinate activities to counter money laundering and terrorist financing with other supervisory authorities , the registrar and law enforcement authorities;
@ref reg 50(1)(b) (src:1694-1696)
GIVEN `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-ordinate activities to counter money laundering and terrorist financing with other supervisory authorities, the registrar and law enforcement authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 50(1)(b) the authority has taken the steps it considers appropriate to co-ordinate activities` MEANS
    IF `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-ordinate activities to counter money laundering and terrorist financing with other supervisory authorities, the registrar and law enforcement authorities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take such steps as it considers appropriate" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 50(1) (src:1694)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 50(1) the authority must take the steps it considers appropriate to co-operate and co-ordinate (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 50(1) co-operate and co-ordinate`

-- "A supervisory authority may take such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with
-- overseas authorities (a) for the purposes of these Regulations, and (b) to ensure the
-- effective supervision of a relevant person to which paragraph (2) applies."
-- src:1698 | (1A) A supervisory authority may take such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with overseas authorities—
-- src:1699 | (a) for the purposes of these Regulations, and
-- src:1700 | (b) to ensure the effective supervision of a relevant person to which paragraph (2) applies.
@ref reg 50(1A) (src:1698-1700)
GIVEN `the steps are for the purposes of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the steps are to ensure the effective supervision of a relevant person to which paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 50(1A) the authority may take such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with overseas authorities` MEANS
    IF `the steps are for the purposes of these Regulations`
       AND `the steps are to ensure the effective supervision of a relevant person to which paragraph (2) applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) for the purposes of these Regulations, and (b) to ensure the effective supervision" -- steps for another purpose are outside the permission
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "This paragraph applies to a relevant person established (a) in the United Kingdom, which has
-- its head office in another country; or (b) in another country but which has its head office
-- in the United Kingdom."
-- src:1701 | (2) This paragraph applies to a relevant person established—
-- src:1702 | (a) in the United Kingdom, which has its head office in another country; or
-- src:1703 | (b) in another country but which has its head office in the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 50(2) (src:1701-1703)
GIVEN `the relevant person is established in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has its head office in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 50(2) paragraph (2) applies to the relevant person` MEANS
    IF `the relevant person is established in the United Kingdom` AND (NOT `the relevant person has its head office in the United Kingdom`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT `the relevant person is established in the United Kingdom`) AND `the relevant person has its head office in the United Kingdom`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): (a) and (b) say two cases to which the paragraph applies and do not say that it applies to no other
         ELSE NOTHING

-- "Co-operation may include the sharing of information which the supervisory authority is not
-- prevented from disclosing, provided that (a) ... equivalent confidentiality; (b) where the
-- information has been received from a third country, it is only disclosed (i) with the express
-- consent ...; and (ii) where appropriate, for the purposes for which it was originally provided."
-- src:1704 | (3) Co-operation may include the sharing of information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing , provided that—
-- src:1705 | (a) any confidential information disclosed to the authority in question will be subject to an obligation of confidentiality equivalent to that provided for in regulation 52A;
-- src:1706 | (b) where the information disclosed has been received from a third country, it is only disclosed—
-- src:1707 | (i) with the express consent of the competent authority or other institution which provided the information; and
-- src:1708 | (ii) where appropriate, for the purposes for which the information was originally provided.
@ref reg 50(3) (src:1704-1708)
GIVEN `it is information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is confidential information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority to which it is disclosed will hold it subject to an obligation of confidentiality equivalent to that in regulation 52A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was received from a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority or other institution which provided it has given its express consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate to confine the disclosure to the purposes for which the information was originally provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is disclosed for the purposes for which it was originally provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 50(3) co-operation may include the sharing of the information` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the sharing of information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing" -- information it is prevented from disclosing is outside the permission
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF ((NOT `it is confidential information`) OR `the authority to which it is disclosed will hold it subject to an obligation of confidentiality equivalent to that in regulation 52A`)
            AND ((NOT `it was received from a third country`)
                 OR (`the competent authority or other institution which provided it has given its express consent`
                     AND ((NOT `it is appropriate to confine the disclosure to the purposes for which the information was originally provided`) OR `it is disclosed for the purposes for which it was originally provided`)))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that" -- paragraph (a) or (b) is not met (Marginal readings, (a))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "For the purposes of this regulation 'overseas authority' means (a) an authority responsible
-- for any of the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive in an EEA state
-- ... in which the relevant person is established or has its head office; and (b) where the
-- relevant person is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA
-- state, an authority in that country which has equivalent functions".  The "and" joins two
-- kinds of authority, so a body is an overseas authority if it is either (fork F2).
-- src:1709 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation “overseas authority” means—
-- src:1710 | (a) an authority responsible for any of the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive in an EEA state ... in which the relevant person is established or has its head office; and
-- src:1711 | (b) where the relevant person is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA state, an authority in that country which has equivalent functions to any of the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive.
@ref reg 50(4) (src:1709-1711)
GIVEN `the body is responsible for any of the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is in an EEA state in which the relevant person is established or has its head office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is in that country and has functions equivalent to any of the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 50(4) the body is an overseas authority` MEANS
    IF `the body is responsible for any of the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive`
       AND `the body is in an EEA state in which the relevant person is established or has its head office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the relevant person is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA state`
            AND `the body is in that country and has functions equivalent to any of the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" -- neither (a) nor (b) is met
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1712 | (4A) A reference to the registrar in this regulation is to the registrar of companies within the meaning of section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006.
@ref reg 50(4A) (src:1712)
GIVEN `the person is the registrar of companies within the meaning of section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 50(4A) the person is the registrar referred to in this regulation` MEANS
    IF `the person is the registrar of companies within the meaning of section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference to the registrar in this regulation is to the registrar of companies within the meaning of section 1060(3)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 51 -- Regulatory information`

-- src:1715 | (1) A supervisory authority within regulation 7 must collect such information as it considers necessary for the purpose of performing its supervisory functions, including the information specified in Schedule 4.
@ref reg 51(1) (src:1715)
GIVEN `the authority is a supervisory authority within regulation 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has collected such information as it considers necessary for the purpose of performing its supervisory functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information collected includes the information specified in Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 51(1) the authority has collected the information it considers necessary, including the information specified in Schedule 4` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the authority is a supervisory authority within regulation 7`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A supervisory authority within regulation 7" -- another body is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it has collected such information as it considers necessary for the purpose of performing its supervisory functions`
            AND `the information collected includes the information specified in Schedule 4`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must collect" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 51(1) (src:1715)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 51(1) the authority must collect the information (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 51(1) collect information`

-- "on request": the duty to provide arises upon the Treasury's request for information it specified;
-- with no request the answer is JUST FALSE (fork F9).
-- src:1716 | (2) A supervisory authority within regulation 7 must on request provide the Treasury with such information collected under paragraph (1) as may be specified by the Treasury, for the purpose of enabling the Treasury to perform its functions under these Regulations.
@ref reg 51(2) (src:1716)
GIVEN `the authority is a supervisory authority within regulation 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Treasury has asked for the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is information collected under paragraph (1) that the Treasury specified for the purpose of performing its functions under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has provided it to the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 51(2) the authority has provided the Treasury with the information on request` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the authority is a supervisory authority within regulation 7`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A supervisory authority within regulation 7" -- another body is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `the Treasury has asked for the information`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on request" -- "on request" is read as "upon request", which counts as "where" (delegated reading (c) of 2026-11-05; fork F9), and there is no request
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF (NOT `it is information collected under paragraph (1) that the Treasury specified for the purpose of performing its functions under these Regulations`)
              -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such information collected under paragraph (1) as may be specified by the Treasury" -- information the Treasury did not specify is outside the duty
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE IF `the authority has provided it to the Treasury`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must on request provide" (Marginal readings, (c))
                   ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 51(2) (src:1716)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 51(2) the authority must provide the Treasury with the information on request (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 51(2) provide the Treasury with information on request`

-- src:1717 | (2A) The Treasury may disclose to the FCA information provided by the supervisory authorities under paragraph (2), provided that the disclosure is made for purposes connected with the effective exercise of—
-- src:1718 | (a) the functions of the Treasury under these Regulations in relation to self-regulatory organisations or under the Oversight of Professional Body Anti-Money Laundering and Counter Terrorist Financing Supervision Regulations 2017 (“the Professional Body Regulations”); or
-- src:1719 | (b) the functions of the FCA under the Professional Body Regulations.
@ref reg 51(2A) (src:1717-1719)
GIVEN `the information was provided by the supervisory authorities under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the Treasury's functions in relation to self-regulatory organisations or under the Professional Body Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the FCA's functions under the Professional Body Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 51(2A) the Treasury may disclose the information to the FCA` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the information was provided by the supervisory authorities under paragraph (2)`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "information provided by the supervisory authorities under paragraph (2)" -- other information is outside the permission
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the Treasury's functions in relation to self-regulatory organisations or under the Professional Body Regulations`
            OR `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the FCA's functions under the Professional Body Regulations`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that the disclosure is made for purposes connected with the effective exercise of" (Marginal readings, (a))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1720 | (3) The Treasury must publish an annual consolidated review of the information provided by the supervisory authorities under paragraph (2).
@ref reg 51(3) (src:1720)
GIVEN `the Treasury has published an annual consolidated review of the information provided by the supervisory authorities under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 51(3) the Treasury has published an annual consolidated review of the information` MEANS
    IF `the Treasury has published an annual consolidated review of the information provided by the supervisory authorities under paragraph (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must publish an annual consolidated review" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 51(3) (src:1720)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 46 act of an authority`
`reg 51(3) the Treasury must publish an annual consolidated review (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 51(3) publish an annual consolidated review`

-- src:1721 | (4) A disclosure made under paragraph (2) or (2A) is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information.
@ref reg 51(4) (src:1721)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure was made under paragraph (2A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 51(4) the disclosure is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure was made under paragraph (2)` OR `the disclosure was made under paragraph (2A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A disclosure made under paragraph (2) or (2A)" -- a disclosure made otherwise is outside the protection
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1722 | (5) Where a disclosure under paragraph (2) or (2A) is made in good faith, no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person by whom, or on whose behalf, it is made.
@ref reg 51(5) (src:1722)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure was made under paragraph (2A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 51(5) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person who made it` MEANS
    IF (`the disclosure was made under paragraph (2)` OR `the disclosure was made under paragraph (2A)`) AND `it was made in good faith`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a disclosure under paragraph (2) or (2A) is made in good faith" -- the condition is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); Marginal readings, (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 52 -- Disclosure by supervisory authorities and other relevant authorities`

-- What a body is, when the question is whether it is a "relevant authority" (reg 52(5)).  One
-- field for each of the seven descriptions; (c) is a MAYBE because "law enforcement authority"
-- is reg 44(10)'s (SEAM S-15).
DECLARE `reg 52(5) description of the body` HAS
    `another supervisory authority`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Treasury`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `reg 44(10) a law enforcement authority`                       IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `an overseas authority within the meaning of regulation 50(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State for purposes connected with the effective exercise of functions under enactments relating to companies, audit and insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the registrar of companies within the meaning of section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1741 | (5) For the purposes of this regulation, “relevant authority” means—
-- src:1742 | (a) another supervisory authority;
-- src:1743 | (b) the Treasury;
-- src:1744 | (c) any law enforcement authority;
-- src:1745 | (d) an overseas authority, within the meaning of regulation 50(4);
-- src:1746 | (e) the Secretary of State for purposes connected with the effective exercise of his or her functions under enactments relating to companies, audit and insolvency;
-- src:1747 | (f) the registrar of companies within the meaning of section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006;
-- src:1748 | (g) the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme, within the meaning of that section.
@ref reg 52(5) (src:1741-1748)
-- SEAM S-15 (asking)
GIVEN body IS A `reg 52(5) description of the body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52(5) the body is a relevant authority` MEANS
    IF body's `another supervisory authority`
       OR body's `the Treasury`
       OR body's `an overseas authority within the meaning of regulation 50(4)`
       OR body's `the Secretary of State for purposes connected with the effective exercise of functions under enactments relating to companies, audit and insolvency`
       OR body's `the registrar of companies within the meaning of section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`
       OR body's `the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER body's `reg 44(10) a law enforcement authority`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a law enforcement authority is reg 44(10)'s answer and it has not been given
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant authority' means" -- the body fits none of (a) to (g)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE

-- "A supervisory authority may disclose to a relevant authority information it holds relevant to
-- its supervisory functions, provided the disclosure is made for purposes connected with the
-- effective exercise of (a) ... (d)".  The rendering shows "..." at the start of (1) and after
-- (b): text removed.
-- src:1724 | (1) ... A supervisory authority may disclose to a relevant authority information it holds relevant to its supervisory functions, provided the disclosure is made for purposes connected with the effective exercise of—
-- src:1725 | (a) the functions of the relevant authority under these Regulations or any other functions related to money laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system;
-- src:1726 | (b) the functions of the law enforcement authority; ...
-- src:1727 | (c) in the case of an overseas authority, the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive, or equivalent functions; or
-- src:1728 | (d) the functions of the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme, within the meaning of that section.
@ref reg 52(1) (src:1724-1728)
GIVEN body IS A `reg 52(5) description of the body`
      `the information is information it holds relevant to its supervisory functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions of the relevant authority under these Regulations or any other functions related to money laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions of the law enforcement authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant authority is an overseas authority and the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive, or equivalent functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions of the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52(1) the supervisory authority may disclose the information to the relevant authority` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the information is information it holds relevant to its supervisory functions`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "information it holds relevant to its supervisory functions" -- other information is outside the permission
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 52(5) the body is a relevant authority` body
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a law enforcement authority is reg 44(10)'s answer and it has not been given
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "disclose to a relevant authority" -- a body that is not a relevant authority is outside the permission
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions of the relevant authority under these Regulations or any other functions related to money laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system`
                OR `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions of the law enforcement authority`
                OR `the relevant authority is an overseas authority and the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive, or equivalent functions`
                OR `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions of the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided the disclosure is made for purposes connected with the effective exercise of" (Marginal readings, (a))
             ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "A relevant authority referred to in paragraph (5)(b), (c), (e), (f) or (g) may disclose to a
-- supervisory authority or another relevant authority information it holds, provided the
-- disclosure is made for purposes connected with (a) the effective exercise of the functions of
-- the supervisory authority or other relevant authority under these Regulations; or (b) money
-- laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system."
-- src:1729 | (1A) A relevant authority referred to in paragraph (5)(b), (c), (e), (f) or (g) may disclose to a supervisory authority or another relevant authority referred to in paragraph (5) information it holds, provided the disclosure is made for purposes connected with—
-- src:1730 | (a) the effective exercise of the functions of the supervisory authority or other relevant authority under these Regulations; or
-- src:1731 | (b) money laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system.
@ref reg 52(1A) (src:1729-1731)
GIVEN body IS A `reg 52(5) description of the body`
      `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions of the supervisory authority or other relevant authority under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for purposes connected with money laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52(1A) the relevant authority may disclose the information to a supervisory authority or another relevant authority` MEANS
    IF body's `the Treasury`
       OR body's `the Secretary of State for purposes connected with the effective exercise of functions under enactments relating to companies, audit and insolvency`
       OR body's `the registrar of companies within the meaning of section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`
       OR body's `the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme`
       OR body's `reg 44(10) a law enforcement authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the disclosure is for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions of the supervisory authority or other relevant authority under these Regulations`
            OR `the disclosure is for purposes connected with money laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided the disclosure is made for purposes connected with" (Marginal readings, (a))
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A relevant authority referred to in paragraph (5)(b), (c), (e), (f) or (g)" -- another supervisory authority, an overseas authority, or a body whose standing as a law enforcement authority is not answered, is outside the permission
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1732 | (1B) Nothing in paragraph (1A) affects the powers of a relevant authority referred to in paragraph (5)(b), (c), (e), (f) or (g) to disclose information to a supervisory authority or other relevant authority apart from this regulation.
@ref reg 52(1B) (src:1732)
GIVEN body IS A `reg 52(5) description of the body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52(1B) paragraph (1A) affects the powers of the relevant authority to disclose information apart from this regulation` MEANS
    IF body's `the Treasury`
       OR body's `the Secretary of State for purposes connected with the effective exercise of functions under enactments relating to companies, audit and insolvency`
       OR body's `the registrar of companies within the meaning of section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`
       OR body's `the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme`
       OR body's `reg 44(10) a law enforcement authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in paragraph (1A) affects the powers of a relevant authority"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a relevant authority referred to in paragraph (5)(b), (c), (e), (f) or (g)" -- another body is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "Information disclosed to a relevant authority under paragraph (1) or (1A) may not be further
-- disclosed by that authority, except (a) ... (e)".
-- src:1733 | (2) Information disclosed to a relevant authority under paragraph (1) or (1A) may not be further disclosed by that authority, except—
-- src:1734 | (a) in accordance with paragraph (1) or (1A);
-- src:1735 | (b) by the FCA to the PRA, where the information concerns a PRA-authorised person or a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person;
-- src:1736 | (c) in the case of an overseas authority, in accordance with any conditions imposed on further disclosure of that information by the supervisory authority which disclosed that information to the overseas authority;
-- src:1737 | (d) with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, any criminal or other enforcement proceedings; or
-- src:1738 | (e) as otherwise required by law.
@ref reg 52(2) (src:1733-1738)
GIVEN `the information was disclosed to the relevant authority under paragraph (1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further disclosure is in accordance with paragraph (1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant authority is the FCA, the recipient is the PRA, and the information concerns a PRA-authorised person or a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant authority is an overseas authority and the further disclosure is in accordance with the conditions imposed by the supervisory authority which disclosed the information to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further disclosure is with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, criminal or other enforcement proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further disclosure is otherwise required by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52(2) the relevant authority may further disclose the information` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the information was disclosed to the relevant authority under paragraph (1) or (1A)`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information disclosed to a relevant authority under paragraph (1) or (1A)" -- other information is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the further disclosure is in accordance with paragraph (1) or (1A)`
            OR `the relevant authority is the FCA, the recipient is the PRA, and the information concerns a PRA-authorised person or a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person`
            OR `the relevant authority is an overseas authority and the further disclosure is in accordance with the conditions imposed by the supervisory authority which disclosed the information to it`
            OR `the further disclosure is with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, criminal or other enforcement proceedings`
            OR `the further disclosure is otherwise required by law`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be further disclosed by that authority, except" -- none of (a) to (e) is met
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1739 | (3) A disclosure made under paragraph (1) or (1A) is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information.
@ref reg 52(3) (src:1739)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure was made under paragraph (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52(3) the disclosure is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure was made under paragraph (1)` OR `the disclosure was made under paragraph (1A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A disclosure made under paragraph (1) or (1A)" -- a disclosure made otherwise is outside the protection
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1740 | (4) Where a disclosure under paragraph (1) or (1A) is made in good faith, no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person by whom, or on whose behalf, it is made.
@ref reg 52(4) (src:1740)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure was made under paragraph (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52(4) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person who made it` MEANS
    IF (`the disclosure was made under paragraph (1)` OR `the disclosure was made under paragraph (1A)`) AND `it was made in good faith`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a disclosure under paragraph (1) or (1A) is made in good faith" -- the condition is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); Marginal readings, (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 52A -- Obligation of confidentiality`

DECLARE `reg 52A act of a person` IS ONE OF
    `reg 52A(1) disclose confidential information received in the course of duties`

-- "No person working for a relevant supervisory authority, or acting on behalf of a relevant
-- supervisory authority (or who has worked or acted for a relevant supervisory authority) may,
-- except in accordance with this regulation, disclose any confidential information received in
-- the course of their duties under these Regulations."  JUST FALSE: the person may not.
-- src:1750 | (1) No person working for a relevant supervisory authority, or acting on behalf of a relevant supervisory authority (or who has worked or acted for a relevant supervisory authority) may, except in accordance with this regulation, disclose any confidential information received in the course of their duties under these Regulations.
@ref reg 52A(1) (src:1750)
GIVEN `the person works or acts, or has worked or acted, for a relevant supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is confidential information received in the course of their duties under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is in accordance with this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52A(1) the person may disclose the confidential information` MEANS
    IF `the person works or acts, or has worked or acted, for a relevant supervisory authority`
       AND `the information is confidential information received in the course of their duties under these Regulations`
    THEN IF `the disclosure is in accordance with this regulation`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in accordance with this regulation" -- a disclosure in accordance with the regulation is outside the prohibition, and the permission is in paragraphs (2) to (5)
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person ... may, except in accordance with this regulation, disclose any confidential information"
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person working for a relevant supervisory authority ... any confidential information received in the course of their duties under these Regulations" -- another person, or other information, is outside the prohibition
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The prohibition of reg 52A(1) asked in its own polarity: does it apply to the disclosure?  "Except in
-- accordance with this regulation" is an "unless": a disclosure in accordance with the regulation is
-- outside the prohibition (JUST FALSE), any other disclosure by such a person of such information is
-- inside it (JUST TRUE).  The reach of the prohibition ("No person working for ...") is a scope limit
-- with no "only", so a person or information outside it is NOTHING (fork F10).
@ref reg 52A(1) (src:1750)
GIVEN `the person works or acts, or has worked or acted, for a relevant supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is confidential information received in the course of their duties under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is in accordance with this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52A(1) the prohibition on disclosing the confidential information applies` MEANS
    IF `the person works or acts, or has worked or acted, for a relevant supervisory authority`
       AND `the information is confidential information received in the course of their duties under these Regulations`
    THEN IF `the disclosure is in accordance with this regulation`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in accordance with this regulation" -- an "unless", read as "if" (fork F10): a disclosure in accordance with the regulation is outside the prohibition
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person working for a relevant supervisory authority ... any confidential information received in the course of their duties under these Regulations" -- another person, or other information, is outside the prohibition
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 52A(1) (src:1750)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 52A act of a person`
`reg 52A(1) the person shall not disclose the confidential information (as a prohibition)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    SHANT `reg 52A(1) disclose confidential information received in the course of duties`

-- "Information referred to in paragraph (1) may be disclosed in summary or aggregate form,
-- provided that no credit institution, financial institution or cryptoasset business is
-- identifiable from the information disclosed."
-- src:1751 | (2) Information referred to in paragraph (1) may be disclosed in summary or aggregate form, provided that no credit institution, financial institution or cryptoasset business is identifiable from the information disclosed.
@ref reg 52A(2) (src:1751)
GIVEN `the information is disclosed in summary or aggregate form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a credit institution, a financial institution or a cryptoasset business is identifiable from the information disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52A(2) the information may be disclosed in summary or aggregate form` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the information is disclosed in summary or aggregate form`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be disclosed in summary or aggregate form" -- disclosure in another form is outside the permission
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a credit institution, a financial institution or a cryptoasset business is identifiable from the information disclosed`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that no credit institution, financial institution or cryptoasset business is identifiable" (Marginal readings, (a))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `reg 52A(3) disclosure of confidential information` HAS
    `the information was received pursuant to these Regulations`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the discharge of its duties under these Regulations`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN -- (a)
    `in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN -- (a)(i)
    `in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to prudential regulation`                      IS A BOOLEAN -- (a)(ii)
    `in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to the supervision of credit institutions, financial institutions and cryptoasset businesses` IS A BOOLEAN -- (a)(iii)
    `in an appeal against a decision of a supervisory authority`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN -- (b)
    `in court proceedings initiated by a relevant supervisory authority in the exercise of those duties, or otherwise relating to its discharge of them` IS A BOOLEAN -- (c)
    `in accordance with sections 17 and 18 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005`                  IS A BOOLEAN -- (d)
    `in accordance with sections 348 and 349 of FSMA as modified by paragraph (3A)`                                IS A BOOLEAN -- (da)
    `in accordance with regulation 52`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN -- (e)

-- "A relevant supervisory authority may disclose confidential information received pursuant to
-- these Regulations (a) ... (e)".  (d) is for the Commissioners as supervisory authority and
-- (da) is for the FCA as supervisory authority.
-- src:1752 | (3) A relevant supervisory authority may disclose confidential information received pursuant to these Regulations—
-- src:1753 | (a) in the discharge of its duties under these Regulations or under other legislation relating to—
-- src:1754 | (i) money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing;
-- src:1755 | (ii) prudential regulation; or
-- src:1756 | (iii) the supervision of credit institutions, financial institutions and cryptoasset businesses;
-- src:1757 | (b) in an appeal against a decision of a supervisory authority;
-- src:1758 | (c) in court proceedings initiated by a relevant supervisory authority in the exercise of the duties referred to in sub-paragraph (a), or otherwise relating to the authority’s discharge of those duties;
-- src:1759 | (d) where the Commissioners are the supervisory authority, in accordance with sections 17 and 18 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005;
-- src:1760 | (da) where the FCA is the supervisory authority, unless disclosure is otherwise permitted by this regulation, in accordance with sections 348 (restrictions on disclosure of confidential information by FCA, PRA etc.) and 349 (exceptions from section 348) of FSMA where those sections shall apply for the purposes of this sub-paragraph subject to the modifications in paragraph (3A);
-- src:1761 | (e) in accordance with regulation 52.
@ref reg 52A(3) (src:1752-1761)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `reg 52A(3) disclosure of confidential information`
      `the authority is a relevant supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners are the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA is the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52A(3) the relevant supervisory authority may disclose the confidential information` MEANS
    IF `the authority is a relevant supervisory authority` AND disclosure's `the information was received pursuant to these Regulations`
    THEN IF disclosure's `in the discharge of its duties under these Regulations`
            OR disclosure's `in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing`
            OR disclosure's `in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to prudential regulation`
            OR disclosure's `in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to the supervision of credit institutions, financial institutions and cryptoasset businesses`
            OR disclosure's `in an appeal against a decision of a supervisory authority`
            OR disclosure's `in court proceedings initiated by a relevant supervisory authority in the exercise of those duties, or otherwise relating to its discharge of them`
            OR (`the Commissioners are the supervisory authority` AND disclosure's `in accordance with sections 17 and 18 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005`)
            OR (`the FCA is the supervisory authority` AND disclosure's `in accordance with sections 348 and 349 of FSMA as modified by paragraph (3A)`)
            OR disclosure's `in accordance with regulation 52`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): (a) to (e) say routes by which the authority may disclose and do not say that it may disclose by no other route; the prohibition is paragraph (1)'s
         ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A relevant supervisory authority may disclose confidential information received pursuant to these Regulations" -- another authority, or other information, is outside the permission
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 348 of FSMA as paragraph (3A) says it is to be read.  A rule of reading, so it is a
-- function over a small representation of what the rule operates on: the provisions of section
-- 348 and of the regulations made under section 349 that the paragraph names.
DECLARE `reg 52A(3A) provision of FSMA` IS ONE OF
    `reg 52A(3A)(a) section 348(1), any reference to a primary recipient`
    `reg 52A(3A)(b)(i) section 348(2)(b), the primary recipient`
    `reg 52A(3A)(b)(ii) section 348(2)(b), the words from ", the PRA" to the end of that subsection`
    `reg 52A(3A)(c) section 348(2A)`
    `reg 52A(3A)(d) section 348(3)(a), this Act`
    `reg 52A(3A)(e) section 348(5) to (8)`
    `reg 52A(3A)(f) regulations under section 349, any reference to primary recipient`
    `reg 52A(3A) any other provision of FSMA`

DECLARE `reg 52A(3A) how the provision is read` IS ONE OF
    `reg 52A(3A) it is omitted`
    `reg 52A(3A) it is read with these words substituted` HAS `the words substituted` IS A STRING

-- src:1762 | (3A) Section 348 of FSMA is to be read as if—
-- src:1763 | (a) in subsection (1), for any reference to “a primary recipient” or “the primary recipient” there were substituted “the FCA”;
-- src:1764 | (b) in subsection (2)(b)—
-- src:1765 | (i) for “the primary recipient” there were substituted “the FCA”;
-- src:1766 | (ii) for the words from “, the PRA” to the end of that subsection there were substituted “under the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017”;
-- src:1767 | (c) subsection (2A) were omitted;
-- src:1768 | (d) in subsection (3)(a), for “this Act” there were substituted “the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017”;
-- src:1769 | (e) subsections (5) to (8) were omitted;
-- src:1770 | (f) any reference to “primary recipient” in regulations made under section 349 of FSMA were a reference to “the FCA”.
@ref reg 52A(3A) (src:1762-1770)
GIVEN provision IS A `reg 52A(3A) provision of FSMA`
GIVETH A MAYBE `reg 52A(3A) how the provision is read`
`reg 52A(3A) section 348 of FSMA is to be read as if` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `reg 52A(3A)(a) section 348(1), any reference to a primary recipient` THEN JUST (`reg 52A(3A) it is read with these words substituted` "the FCA")
    WHEN `reg 52A(3A)(b)(i) section 348(2)(b), the primary recipient` THEN JUST (`reg 52A(3A) it is read with these words substituted` "the FCA")
    WHEN `reg 52A(3A)(b)(ii) section 348(2)(b), the words from ", the PRA" to the end of that subsection` THEN JUST (`reg 52A(3A) it is read with these words substituted` "under the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017")
    WHEN `reg 52A(3A)(c) section 348(2A)` THEN JUST `reg 52A(3A) it is omitted`
    WHEN `reg 52A(3A)(d) section 348(3)(a), this Act` THEN JUST (`reg 52A(3A) it is read with these words substituted` "the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017")
    WHEN `reg 52A(3A)(e) section 348(5) to (8)` THEN JUST `reg 52A(3A) it is omitted`
    WHEN `reg 52A(3A)(f) regulations under section 349, any reference to primary recipient` THEN JUST (`reg 52A(3A) it is read with these words substituted` "the FCA")
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (3A) names six places in section 348 and in the regulations under section 349 and says nothing of any other provision of FSMA
    WHEN `reg 52A(3A) any other provision of FSMA` THEN NOTHING

-- "This regulation does not prevent the exchange of information between (a) any authority in the
-- United Kingdom responsible for the supervision of a credit institution, a financial institution
-- or a cryptoasset business ... (a 'UK authority') and another UK authority; (b) a UK authority
-- and a competent authority in a third country supervising any credit or financial institution
-- or cryptoasset business in accordance with (i) the fourth money laundering directive ...; (ii)
-- laws imposing requirements ... which have an equivalent effect".  JUST FALSE: it does not
-- prevent.
-- src:1771 | (4) This regulation does not prevent the exchange of information between—
-- src:1772 | (a) any authority in the United Kingdom responsible for the supervision of a credit institution, a financial institution or a cryptoasset business in accordance with these Regulations or other law relating to credit institutions, financial institutions or cryptoasset businesses (a “UK authority”) and another UK authority;
-- src:1773 | (b) a UK authority and a competent authority in a third country supervising any credit or financial institution or cryptoasset business in accordance with—
-- src:1774 | (i) the fourth money laundering directive or other legislative acts relating to credit institutions, financial institutions or cryptoasset businesses;
-- src:1775 | (ii) laws imposing requirements on credit institutions, financial institutions or cryptoasset businesses which have an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive.
@ref reg 52A(4) (src:1771-1775)
GIVEN `the exchange is between two UK authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exchange is between a UK authority and a competent authority in a third country supervising a credit or financial institution or cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third-country authority supervises in accordance with the fourth money laundering directive or other legislative acts relating to those institutions or businesses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third-country authority supervises in accordance with laws imposing requirements which have an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52A(4) this regulation prevents the exchange of information between the authorities` MEANS
    IF `the exchange is between two UK authorities`
       OR (`the exchange is between a UK authority and a competent authority in a third country supervising a credit or financial institution or cryptoasset business`
           AND (`the third-country authority supervises in accordance with the fourth money laundering directive or other legislative acts relating to those institutions or businesses`
                OR `the third-country authority supervises in accordance with laws imposing requirements which have an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation does not prevent the exchange of information between"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not prevent the exchange of information between (a) ... (b) ..." -- an exchange between other bodies is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1776 | (5) Confidential information may only be exchanged under paragraph (4) if the authority to which the information is provided agrees to hold it subject to an obligation of confidentiality equivalent to that set out in paragraph (1).
@ref reg 52A(5) (src:1776)
GIVEN `the information is exchanged under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority to which it is provided agrees to hold it subject to an obligation of confidentiality equivalent to that set out in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52A(5) the confidential information may be exchanged under paragraph (4)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the information is exchanged under paragraph (4)`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "exchanged under paragraph (4)" -- an exchange made otherwise is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the authority to which it is provided agrees to hold it subject to an obligation of confidentiality equivalent to that set out in paragraph (1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be exchanged under paragraph (4) if"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1777 | (6) Nothing in this regulation affects the disclosure of confidential information in accordance with regulations made under section 349 (exceptions from section 348) of FSMA .
@ref reg 52A(6) (src:1777)
GIVEN `the disclosure is in accordance with regulations made under section 349 of FSMA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52A(6) this regulation affects the disclosure of confidential information in accordance with regulations made under section 349 of FSMA` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is in accordance with regulations made under section 349 of FSMA`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this regulation affects the disclosure of confidential information in accordance with regulations made under section 349"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with regulations made under section 349" -- a disclosure made otherwise is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "a 'relevant supervisory authority' is a supervisory authority which is responsible for the
-- supervision of credit institutions, financial institutions or cryptoasset businesses."
-- src:1778 | (7) For the purposes of this regulation, a “relevant supervisory authority” is a supervisory authority which is responsible for the supervision of credit institutions, financial institutions or cryptoasset businesses.
@ref reg 52A(7) (src:1778)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority is responsible for the supervision of credit institutions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority is responsible for the supervision of financial institutions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority is responsible for the supervision of cryptoasset businesses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52A(7) the supervisory authority is a relevant supervisory authority` MEANS
    IF `the supervisory authority is responsible for the supervision of credit institutions`
       OR `the supervisory authority is responsible for the supervision of financial institutions`
       OR `the supervisory authority is responsible for the supervision of cryptoasset businesses`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'relevant supervisory authority' is a supervisory authority which is responsible for" (a definition by "is", read as closed: marginal reading (g), NOTES.md)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 52B -- Obligation of confidentiality: offence`

-- src:1780 | (1) Any person who discloses information in contravention of regulation 52A is guilty of an offence.
@ref reg 52B(1) (src:1780)
GIVEN `the person discloses information in contravention of regulation 52A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52B(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person discloses information in contravention of regulation 52A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who discloses information in contravention of regulation 52A" -- a person who does not is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `reg 52B(2) mode of conviction` IS ONE OF
    `reg 52B(2)(a) on summary conviction`
    `reg 52B(2)(b) on conviction on indictment`

DECLARE `reg 52B(2) limit on the fine` IS ONE OF
    `reg 52B(2) a fine, and the regulation states no limit on it`
    `reg 52B(2)(a)(ii) a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum`

DECLARE `reg 52B(2) the most the court may impose` HAS
    `term of imprisonment in months, not exceeding`   IS A NUMBER
    `fine`                                            IS A `reg 52B(2) limit on the fine`

-- Summary conviction: three months, and a fine (England and Wales: no limit stated; Scotland and
-- Northern Ireland: not exceeding the statutory maximum).  Conviction on indictment: two years or
-- a fine (no limit stated).  The "or both" and "or" alternatives are the court's choice among
-- these ceilings; the function gives the ceilings.
-- src:1781 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable—
-- src:1782 | (a) on summary conviction—
-- src:1783 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both,
-- src:1784 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both;
-- src:1785 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or to a fine or to both.
@ref reg 52B(2) (src:1781-1785)
GIVEN mode IS A `reg 52B(2) mode of conviction`
      part IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
GIVETH A `reg 52B(2) the most the court may impose`
`reg 52B(2) the most a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable to` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `reg 52B(2)(a) on summary conviction` THEN
        CONSIDER part
        WHEN `England and Wales` THEN `reg 52B(2) the most the court may impose` OF 3, `reg 52B(2) a fine, and the regulation states no limit on it`
        WHEN `Scotland` THEN `reg 52B(2) the most the court may impose` OF 3, `reg 52B(2)(a)(ii) a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum`
        WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN `reg 52B(2) the most the court may impose` OF 3, `reg 52B(2)(a)(ii) a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum`
    WHEN `reg 52B(2)(b) on conviction on indictment` THEN `reg 52B(2) the most the court may impose` OF 24, `reg 52B(2) a fine, and the regulation states no limit on it`

-- "(3) In proceedings for an offence under this regulation, it is a defence for the accused to
-- prove (a) that the accused did not know and had no reason to suspect that the information was
-- confidential information; ... (b) that the accused took all reasonable precautions and
-- exercised all due diligence".  The rendering shows "..." where the word joining (a) to (b) was
-- removed.  The text does not choose between "or" and "and": with both proved the defence holds
-- on either reading, with neither proved it holds on neither, and with one proved the answer is
-- NOTHING (fork F8).
-- src:1786 | (3) In proceedings for an offence under this regulation, it is a defence for the accused to prove—
-- src:1787 | (a) that the accused did not know and had no reason to suspect that the information was confidential information; ...
-- src:1788 | (b) that the accused took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence.
@ref reg 52B(3) (src:1786-1788)
GIVEN `the accused proves that the accused did not know and had no reason to suspect that the information was confidential information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused proves that the accused took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 52B(3) it is a defence for the accused` MEANS
    IF `the accused proves that the accused did not know and had no reason to suspect that the information was confidential information`
       AND `the accused proves that the accused took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the accused proves that the accused did not know and had no reason to suspect that the information was confidential information`
            OR `the accused proves that the accused took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence`
         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the word joining (a) to (b) is blank in this rendering, so the text does not say whether one limb or both must be proved
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for the accused to prove" -- neither limb is proved, so this provision gives no defence on these facts (delegated reading (b) of 2026-11-05)
         ELSE JUST FALSE
